          "text": "{\"caseId\":\"V4-C12\",\"actualMission\":\"Reconcile Mica-4's four ledger states, classify the blocking conflict, and select the smallest authorized exact-frame qualification step without importing Mica-3 authority.\",\"finishLine\":\"Mica-4's scheduled cold-flex observation is conducted on the retained qualification frame and its actual result is recorded against Mica-4; certification and placement remain separate later states.\",\"classificationAction\":\"CLASSIFY_FAILURE\",\"failureClass\":\"CURRENT_FRAME_QUALIFICATION_INCOMPLETE\",\"memoryMatchClass\":null,\"dossierEvaluation\":\"BOUNDED_FAIL\",\"nextAction\":\"ADVANCE_WITHIN_EXISTING_AUTHORITY\",\"evidenceReferences\":[\"O01\",\"O02\",\"O03\",\"H01\",\"H02\",\"H03\",\"H04\",\"E01\",\"E02\",\"E03\",\"E04\",\"E05\"],\"factualFindings\":[\"Workshop ledger: Mica-4 has signed fabrication release.\",\"Qualification ledger: Mica-4 has a witnessed passing static-load entry, but its cold-flex observation is recorded as not performed.\",\"Trial summary: the cold-flex language cites the retired Mica-3 archive, not a Mica-4 specimen record.\",\"Certification ledger: no Mica-4 certificate entry exists.\",\"Field-placement ledger: no Mica-4 placement entry exists.\",\"Mica-4 changes the lower-joint angle from Mica-3, and the retained Mica-4 frame is available for the scheduled cold-flex observation.\"],\"inferences\":[\"Fabrication release does not complete Mica-4 qualification.\",\"The Mica-3 summary and certificate cannot satisfy the missing exact-frame Mica-4 observation.\",\"The absent certification and placement entries are downstream consequences of incomplete qualification, not presently certificate-issuance or placement-record gaps.\"],\"conclusion\":\"Mica-4 is fabrication-released but not fully qualified, certified, or placed. The controlling conflict is CURRENT_FRAME_QUALIFICATION_INCOMPLETE, and the authorized cold-flex observation is the bounded advancing step.\",\"earliestSharedCausalBoundary\":\"The geometry boundary at the changed Mica-4 lower-joint angle; from that point Mica-4 requires its own exact-frame qualification evidence and cannot inherit Mica-3 authority.\",\"completeDefectClass\":\"Missing required Mica-4 exact-frame cold-flex observation, with certification and field placement consequently unopened.\",\"safeIndependentContinuation\":\"Conduct only the scheduled Mica-4 cold-flex observation on the retained qualification frame and record the actual result in the qualification ledger; preserve certification and placement as later separate decisions.\",\"retainedEvidenceSufficient\":true,\"repeatedLoopDetected\":false,\"smallestAdvancingAction\":\"Conduct the scheduled cold-flex observation on the retained Mica-4 qualification frame and record its actual result against Mica-4.\",\"authorityClass\":\"NO_NEW_AUTHORITY\",\"authorizationBasis\":\"The current authorization expressly permits the scheduled Mica-4 cold-flex observation and recording its actual result; E05 confirms the laboratory steward may conduct it.\",\"prohibitedOperations\":[\"Issue a Mica-4 certificate before qualification closes.\",\"Place Mica-4 in field service.\",\"Apply the Mica-3 certificate to the changed Mica-4 frame.\"],\"uncertainties\":[\"The outcome of the Mica-4 cold-flex observation is not yet known.\",\"Whether Mica-4 will later qualify for council certification depends on the recorded observation result.\",\"No future certification or placement decision is established by the current packet.\"],\"boundedRationaleSummary\":\"Exact-frame qualification requires both static-load and cold-flex records. Mica-4 has only the former, while the cited cold-flex material belongs to changed Mica-3 geometry. The defect is bounded to incomplete current-frame qualification, and an expressly authorized evidence-producing step remains available.\"}"
